<body><h1>ANSWER KEY — Set 2  <em>(grader only)</em></h1>
<p>Rubric per question: <strong>Route/action (4) · Policy stated (3) · Trap avoided (3)</strong> unless noted.</p>
<hr>
<p><strong>Q1 — Marked delivered, not received.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Marked-delivered / lost. <strong>Action:</strong> Empathize; verify the shipping address on file and the carrier's delivery scan. Advise checking with neighbors/household and around the property, and (for USPS/UPS) that a carrier claim/investigation may be opened. Escalate for a reship-or-refund decision per policy rather than promising one instantly.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising an immediate free reship or refund before verifying the delivery scan/address. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q2 — Order status, team kit.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Order status / processing time. <strong>Action:</strong> Confirm the order is "Awaiting Fulfillment." Quote the <strong>~5-week</strong> processing time for mandatory team kits; state we do <strong>not</strong> offer expedited shipping and orders are worked in the order received; they'll get a tracking email when it ships (allow 1–3 business days shipping after).</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising an ETA not confirmed from the system, or quoting the wrong timeline. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q3 — We shipped wrong size (Capelli error).</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Wrong item received. <strong>Action:</strong> This is <strong>Capelli's error</strong> (order says Large, we sent Medium). Request an <strong>evidence photo</strong> of the wrong item (showing size tag), then ship a <strong>replacement in the correct/ordered size</strong> (Large). Use the quality/apology opener.</li><li><strong>Trap (auto-fail):</strong> treating it as a customer-fault return, or replacing with no photo. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q4 — Personalized/customized item return.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Customized item return. <strong>Action:</strong> <strong>Personalized products (name/number) are not returnable or exchangeable</strong> — unless Capelli made an error (not the case here). Politely explain the personalization policy. No exchange.</li><li><strong>Trap (auto-fail):</strong> accepting a personalized item as a normal return, or offering an exchange. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q5 — Refund status follow-up.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Refund request (status). <strong>Action:</strong> Refunds take ~24h to process and <strong>3–5 business days</strong> to appear, showing as <strong>"CAPELLI SPORT"</strong>. If it's past that window, tell them you're checking with the refunds team and will follow up — do <strong>not</strong> promise a new date until confirmed. Own the follow-up.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> inventing a new refund date; naming the internal refunds team (ROLO) to the customer. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q6 — Phone checkout / cart button.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Website issue. <strong>Action:</strong> On a phone held <strong>vertically</strong>, the CART button doesn't show; turn the phone <strong>horizontal</strong> and scroll to the top to see CART + item count, then tap it to check out. Offer further help if still stuck. (Also: mandatory-kit items must stay in the cart — removing a required item breaks checkout.)</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> telling them the site is broken / escalating instead of giving the known fix. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q7 — Player link (needs own).</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Player link (club-managed). <strong>Action:</strong> Player links are managed by the <strong>club</strong> — we can't create them from outside. Direct the customer to their coach/club administrator to have the child's name/email added to the correct roster; then we can help. If the link is already in our database, provide it.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising to generate a link yourself. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q8 — OOS, needs alternative.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Out of stock. <strong>Action:</strong> Confirm OOS with no firm restock date; offer an <strong>alternative size or color</strong> if available, or <strong>cancel + refund</strong>, or <strong>wait</strong>. Let them choose. Can email Planning to replenish and advise once restocked.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising a firm restock date, or shipping an alternative without confirming the customer wants it. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q9 — Complimentary hoodie charged.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Escalation. <strong>Action:</strong> This is a <strong>known club-wide billing issue</strong> — escalate to the internal team/manager; reply that the correct department is engaged; set <strong>Open + internal note</strong>. Do not refund on the spot without the escalation.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> naming the internal contact (Dan) to the customer, or promising the refund before escalation. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q10 — Multi-issue.</strong> Full credit = all three routed correctly (≈3.3 each):</p>
<ol><li><strong>No confirmation / order status</strong> → check the order in the system; if placed, confirm status + processing timeline; if truly no order exists, advise it may not have gone through.</li><li><strong>Can't access Lightning FC store</strong> → club-managed access; direct to coach/club admin; never share a password.</li><li><strong>Add a keeper jersey</strong> → <strong>cannot add to an existing order</strong>; place a <strong>new order</strong>; as a one-time courtesy, reply with the new order # so shipping can be refunded.</li></ol>
<ul><li><strong>Trap:</strong> merging these into one wrong resolution, or offering to add the jersey to the existing order. <em>(10)</em></li></ul>
<hr>
